a) Ontology in final solution?
Yes - Greg indicated that ontological aspects have importance. The semantic layer is core architecture, not an add-on. Without it, predictive models cannot access integrated data.
b) Scalability to other parts/engines?
Yes. We're building generic frameworks and reusable patterns. Current roadmap: 1 part (now) → 10 parts (6 months) → 50+ parts (12 months) → full system (24 months). The methodology applies to any engine type.
c) Extension to other businesses?
Yes. Using industry-standard approaches (BFO/IOF ontologies) and business-friendly frameworks. Any business with complex systems and dispersed data can leverage this.
Bottom line: We're creating scalable semantic infrastructure that transforms manual data integration into automated intelligence. This investment builds capability across all product lines.
